<div data-cgap-sector="Auto Repair, Tire &amp; Collision" data-cgap-term="auto shop"></div><p class="lead">Most shop injuries happen at the same handful of spots: under a lift that was not set on its locks, beside a tire changer or inflation cage, at a parts washer, and now around hybrid and EV battery work. These signs are written for those exact spots.</p><p>You will find signs for two-post, four-post and in-ground lifts, tire changers and balancers, alignment racks, brake lathes, engine hoists, exhaust extraction, used oil tanks, frame machines and paint booths. Each one is 8x12 aluminum with pre-drilled holes for a column, wall or cage.</p><h2>What to post, and where</h2><div class="il-areas"><div class="il-area"><h3>Tire changer</h3><p>66 signs written for this equipment. Typical spot: On the changer column beside the bead breaker arm at eye level.</p><ul><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-tire-changer-bead-breaker-arm-sign-cgap-c01075-812">Tire Changer Bead Breaker Arm</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-tire-changer-daily-check-board-sign-cgap-n01075-812">Tire Changer Daily Check Board</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-tire-changer-bead-breaker-sign-cgap-w00595-812">Tire Changer Bead Breaker</a></li><li><span data-s="SAFETY FIRST">SAFETY FIRST</span><a href="/products/safety-first-tire-changer-station-sign-cgap-i01075-812">Tire Changer Station</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Two-post vehicle lift</h3><p>51 signs written for this equipment. Typical spot: Mount on the column at head height where techs walk beside a raised vehicle.</p><ul><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-two-post-lift-raised-arms-sign-cgap-c01073-812">Two-Post Lift Raised Arms</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-two-post-lift-arm-pads-sign-cgap-n01073-812">Two-Post Lift Arm Pads</a></li><li><span data-s="SAFETY FIRST">SAFETY FIRST</span><a href="/products/safety-first-two-post-lift-daily-check-sign-cgap-i01073-812">Two-Post Lift Daily Check</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-two-post-lift-arm-restraint-sign-cgap-c01208-812">Two-Post Lift Arm Restraint</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Used oil and antifreeze tank</h3><p>43 signs written for this equipment. Typical spot: On the tank next to the fill funnel.</p><ul><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-used-oil-tank-fill-funnel-sign-cgap-c18332-812">Used Oil Tank Fill Funnel</a></li><li><span data-s="SAFETY FIRST">SAFETY FIRST</span><a href="/products/safety-first-used-oil-tank-sign-cgap-i21493-812">Used Oil Tank</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-used-oil-tank-gauge-sign-cgap-c18463-812">Used Oil Tank Gauge</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-used-oil-pump-hose-sign-cgap-c18594-812">Used Oil Pump Hose</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Vehicle exhaust extraction system</h3><p>40 signs written for this equipment. Typical spot: On the ceiling rail or wall near the hose drop.</p><ul><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-exhaust-hose-drop-sign-cgap-c12590-812">Exhaust Hose Drop</a></li><li><span data-s="SAFETY FIRST">SAFETY FIRST</span><a href="/products/safety-first-exhaust-hose-reel-sign-cgap-i14731-812">Exhaust Hose Reel</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-exhaust-hose-on-floor-sign-cgap-c12725-812">Exhaust Hose On Floor</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-exhaust-nozzle-tailpipe-sign-cgap-c13060-812">Exhaust Nozzle Tailpipe</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Wheel balancer</h3><p>39 signs written for this equipment. Typical spot: On the top or side of the balancer hood.</p><ul><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-wheel-balancer-hood-sign-cgap-c06395-812">Wheel Balancer Hood</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-wheel-balancer-calibration-record-sign-cgap-n06125-812">Wheel Balancer Calibration Record</a></li><li><span data-s="SAFETY FIRST">SAFETY FIRST</span><a href="/products/safety-first-wheel-balancer-sign-cgap-i05790-812">Wheel Balancer</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-wheel-balancer-spinning-wheel-sign-cgap-c06530-812">Wheel Balancer Spinning Wheel</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Alignment rack</h3><p>37 signs written for this equipment. Typical spot: On the floor stanchion beside the approach ramps of the alignment rack.</p><ul><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-alignment-rack-drive-on-ramps-sign-cgap-c01074-812">Alignment Rack Drive-On Ramps</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-alignment-rack-turn-plates-sign-cgap-n01074-812">Alignment Rack Turn Plates</a></li><li><span data-s="SAFETY FIRST">SAFETY FIRST</span><a href="/products/safety-first-alignment-rack-runways-sign-cgap-i01074-812">Alignment Rack Runways</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-alignment-rack-runway-edge-sign-cgap-c01209-812">Alignment Rack Runway Edge</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Transmission jack</h3><p>36 signs written for this equipment. Typical spot: On the wall or post where the jack is parked.</p><ul><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-transmission-jack-handle-sign-cgap-c15607-812">Transmission Jack Handle</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-transmission-jack-pre-use-check-sign-cgap-n19390-812">Transmission Jack Pre-Use Check</a></li><li><span data-s="SAFETY FIRST">SAFETY FIRST</span><a href="/products/safety-first-transmission-jack-capacity-sign-cgap-i18466-812">Transmission Jack Capacity</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-transmission-jack-saddle-strap-sign-cgap-c15741-812">Transmission Jack Saddle Strap</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Hybrid and EV high-voltage service area</h3><p>33 signs written for this equipment. Typical spot: Mount on the PPE rack at the EV bay at eye level.</p><ul><li><span data-s="SAFETY FIRST">SAFETY FIRST</span><a href="/products/safety-first-ev-face-shield-sign-cgap-i10030-812">EV Face Shield</a></li><li><span data-s="SAFETY FIRST">SAFETY FIRST</span><a href="/products/safety-first-ev-insulated-tools-sign-cgap-i10165-812">EV Insulated Tools</a></li><li><span data-s="SAFETY FIRST">SAFETY FIRST</span><a href="/products/safety-first-ev-insulated-tool-return-sign-cgap-i10300-812">EV Insulated Tool Return</a></li><li><span data-s="SAFETY FIRST">SAFETY FIRST</span><a href="/products/safety-first-ev-service-disconnect-sign-cgap-i10435-812">EV Service Disconnect</a></li></ul></div></div><h2>Common questions</h2><div class="il-faq"><details><summary>Do you have signs for EV and hybrid service bays?</summary><p>Yes. There are signs for high-voltage service areas, battery disconnect steps and keeping untrained staff clear while a vehicle is being worked on.</p></details><details><summary>What should be posted at a vehicle lift?</summary><p>Typical postings cover setting the arm pads and locks before going under, rated capacity, and keeping the area clear while raising or lowering. Search &quot;two-post lift&quot; to see the options.</p></details><details><summary>Can I buy a set for the whole shop?</summary><p>Use the Sign Finder, tick the signs you want and add them all to the cart at once.</p></details></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Do you have signs for EV and hybrid service bays?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. There are signs for high-voltage service areas, battery disconnect steps and keeping untrained staff clear while a vehicle is being worked on."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What should be posted at a vehicle lift?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Typical postings cover setting the arm pads and locks before going under, rated capacity, and keeping the area clear while raising or lowering. Search \"two-post lift\" to see the options."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can I buy a set for the whole shop?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Use the Sign Finder, tick the signs you want and add them all to the cart at once."}}]}</script>